d +8.25\u20139.25%)\n  3. Medicare Cap accrual (budget $7\u20139.5M FY2026)\n  4. Roto-Rooter EBITDA margin (guided 21.5\u201322.5%)\n  5. Adjusted EPS vs guidance ($25.00\u2013$25.75)\n  6. Share count (quarterly); SBC (annual 10-K)\n  7. Activists/Barington filings (13D amendments)\n\u2022 Downgrade triggers:\n  \u2022 Two consecutive misses on ADC or margin \u2192 conviction \u22122\n  \u2022 Adjusted EPS below $24.50 (FY2026) \u2192 re-evaluate\n  \u2022 Cap accrual > $15M \u2192 re-evaluate immediately\n  \u2022 WACC (10Y) > 5.2% \u2192 re-run DCF\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 9. RED TEAM & ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 9-1. Short Thesis (5\u20137 bullets)\n1. VITAS's +11.9% revenue is INFLATED by a 455bps Medicare-Cap contra-\n   revenue tailwind. Ex-cap growth is ~8% and cap debt has a 5-year\n   lifespan (CMS settles caps with interest); a reversal is inevitable.\n2. Adjusted EPS excludes SBC (2026E \u2248 $3.50/share, ~14% of EPS).\n   True economic EPS is ~$22 \u2014 today's P/E is ~24.5x, not 21.3x.\n3. Roto-Rooter marketing spend is rising (+11.3% SG&A in Q2) while\n   EBITDA was FLAT and margin fell 77bps. Residential revenue +1.7% \u2014\n   heading toward stall-out.\n4. A two-segment holding co with no synergies = conglomerate discount.\n   Barington's campaign only highlights that management under-delivers\n   without external pressure.\n5. Medicare is the sole payor for 2/3 of revenue. CMS can cut rates or\n   tighten cap rules at any time; even the FY2027 +2.3% was below\n   current cost inflation (hospice labor costs).\n6. Stock trades at a 52-week high ($553) despite FY2025 GAAP EPS going\n   DOWN from $22.81 to $18.35 (adjusted $21.55). \"Recovery\" is already\n   priced.\n7. If growth normalizes to 4% and multiple compresses to 16x, the stock\n   is $430 \u2014 a 20% downside.\n\nStep 9-2. Logic Combat\n\u2022 Long score: 12.5/15 (quality, valuation 19%, catalysts, execution).\n\u2022 Short score: 10/15 (cap-recency issue, SBC, margin, single-payor).\n\u2022 Gap = 2.5 > 2 \u2192 conviction holds, but shaved \u22121 \u2192 11.5/15 HIGH.\n\nStep 9-3. Adversarial Data\n\u2022 Activist Barington (public, July 2026) \u2014 \"reduce costs, strategic review,\n  board refresh.\" [Actual \u2014 Bloomberg; Barington site]\n\u2022 2025 cyberattack exposing PHI \u2014 litigation/fine exposure, amount\n  [Unconfirmed]\n\u2022 No short-seller report (Hindenburg/Muddy Waters) found on CHE.\n\nStep 9-4. Killed Arguments\n\u2022 \"Dual business is a strong moat\" \u2014 KILLED: two unrelated businesses\n  create no moat; survivorship does not equal advantage. It only\n  provides diversification. The moat is narrow, not wide.\n\u2022 \"Activist will unlock massive value immediately\" \u2014 KILLED as a CORE\n  scenario: Barington's battle is months-to-years; value-unlock is a\n  Bull-case optionality (25%), not Base.\n\u2022 \"Low institutional ownership means under-owned\" \u2014 KILLED with\n  caveat: 1.09% is likely a stale/incomplete 13F aggregation; do not\n  rely on it.\n\u2022 CONDEMNED-to-revisit: \"Near-term 8% growth is sustainable 5 years out.\"\n  This is my key assumption; will be re-validated after every quarter.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\